  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday night through Sunday)\nIssued at 128 AM CDT Mon Sep 21 2026\n\nRidging will become better established over the area Wednesday and \nthrough the second half of the week, lowering rain chances. As a \nsteady easterly surface flow sets up over the area, warmth will \nremain elevated with humid conditions, resulting in continued above \naverage and hot daytime temperatures, heat indices, and muggy \novernight conditions through the week. Rain chances will likely \nremain limited to spotty and brief coastal showers and weak \nisentropic lift closer to the Rio Grande. A drier airmass may filter \ninto the area from the northeast Friday/Saturday, which could bring \ndown dew points and overnight temperatures slightly. Overall, \nensembles and statistical guidance do show slight downward trends in \ntemperatures towards the weekend, but these depictions broadly don't \nshow much of a meaningful change from the current streak of hot \nweather within the next seven days.",
